  <prompt>Owner 2026-10-08 (#1401): "we need our canonical solution(s) and don't use others that are created/used/managed by dev team." Every environment — customer stamps and Spaarke's own — gets only the canonical SpaarkeMaster built by CI from git.</prompt>

  <goal>
    `Deploy-Release.ps1` Phase 3 imports SpaarkeMaster from the CI-published store (218d's manifest + versioned zips), with
    the package type per Spaarke environment from `config/environments.json` (managed by default, unmanaged only where the
    owner says so — D8), the same refusals as H6 (type switch, downgrade) and a post-import check of ismanaged + version.
    `Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1` and its 9-solution list are retired; every caller and pointer (`Provision-Customer.ps1`
    step 7, `Load-DemoSampleData.ps1`, `scripts/README.md`, the deploy-new-release skill) is updated or removed.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>ISS-005 (notes/defer-issues.md): Phase 3 still runs Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1, whose list names 9 solutions (6 exist nowhere) and whose zip filter accepts every zip. 218b retired the list for H6 only; 218d makes CI the only producer of the package.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>scripts/Deploy-Release.ps1</file>
      <file>scripts/Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1</file>
      <file>scripts/Provision-Customer.ps1</file>
