  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/t218-plan.md</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SolutionImport/DataverseWebApiSolutionImporter.cs (the reference for manifest parsing, refusals and the async import + poll)</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-10-08">No environment imports a solution the dev team creates or manages by hand; only the CI-published SpaarkeMaster.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D8">Managed by default; unmanaged only by an explicit per-environment setting.</constraint>
    <constraint source="live">Any import into a live Spaarke environment (dev, demo) needs the owner's OK per action.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add a per-environment `solutionPackageType` to config/environments.json; read it in Deploy-Release Phase 3.</step>
    <step order="2">Phase 3: read the manifest from the artifact store, refuse type switch / downgrade against the installed package, import async + poll, verify ismanaged + version.</step>
    <step order="3">Retire Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1; update or remove every caller and pointer; update the skill and the runbook.</step>
    <step order="4">-WhatIf run against demo (read-only); owner OK → real release to demo; close ISS-005 and #1401.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep finds no caller of Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1 and no 9-solution list in scripts/ or .claude/skills/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Deploy-Release -WhatIf against demo names exactly SpaarkeMaster {version} ({type}) from the manifest.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Phase 3 refuses a managed→unmanaged switch and a downgrade (Pester test with a fake installed package).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    <note date="2026-10-08">CODE COMPLETE (SESSION 44) — open only for AC2 (the live -WhatIf against demo naming SpaarkeMaster {version} (unmanaged)), which needs the first CI publish (after PR #1365 merges + owner OK). Commits 8350f27bc (implementation), 4a0b711b6 (review fixes).
    - scripts/solution-authoring/Import-SpaarkeMasterPackage.ps1: manifest from the store → installed package → Resolve-PackageImportPlan (H6's rules, version validated first) → pac solution import --async --force-overwrite --activate-plugins [--stage-and-upgrade managed upgrade] [--publish-changes unmanaged] → read back version + type. Operator's own az/pac identity; refuses the authoring environment (host compare incl. .api.).
    - Deploy-Release Phase 3 typed by config/environments.json solutionPackageType: dev none (authoring), demo unmanaged (demo holds SpaarkeMaster 1.0.0.0 unmanaged, read 2026-10-08; switching = rebuild, owner decision); missing = refused. -ClientSecret ignored with a warning. Provision-Customer step 7 switched (documents its two identities). Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1 deleted; ADR-027 MUSTs; skill + docs updated (no downgrade = roll forward; U-CB-1's nonexistent --allow-destructive flag corrected).
    - Verified: Pester 39/39; read-only -WhatIf against demo + the real store refuses the pre-T218 manifest (SpaarkeMaster 1.1.0.0 with no managed/unmanagedBlobName) with a clear message; dev refused (also the .api. URL form). AC1 met (grep: no caller, no 9-solution list in scripts/ or .claude/skills/). AC3 met (Pester: type switch both ways, downgrade).
    QUALITY GATES: one full review pass — no F1; F2 fixed: H6's import options (--force-overwrite, --activate-plugins), version validated before install, fresh token per read, ADR-027 interim-path wording, doc drift (U-CB-1, matrix, inventory, README, multi-env guide). KNOWN LIMITS: zip checksums not verified (H6 neither); refusals tested at plan level, not through Phase 3 wiring; demo also carries hand-installed dev-team solutions (harmless; nothing but SpaarkeMaster is imported there now).</note>
  </notes>
